  "takeaway": "Boston blew a 21-point halftime lead and trailed 92–91 in the fourth, then Derrick White's and-one keyed a 7–0 run that held off Milwaukee. Without a resting Jayson Tatum, the Celtics stayed perfect at home at 5–0.",
  "report": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "BOS 28, MIL 14",
        "text": "Sam Hauser hit threes on Boston's first two shots, and Paul George played the whole quarter for 10 points and 3 steals. Mitchell Robinson grabbed 6 rebounds in five minutes off the bench."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "BOS 62, MIL 41",
        "text": "Boston led by as many as 22. The Celtics went 10-of-17 from three in the half, with the bench 5-for-5, including Luka Garza 3-for-3. Payton Pritchard briefly left with a cut on his nose and returned."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "text": "Milwaukee opened on a 24–12 run to get within 74–65 with 6:02 left, with Tyler Herro scoring 18 of his 25 in the quarter as the Bucks went 6-of-8 from three. Baylor Scheierman's back-to-back threes pushed the lead back to 13, and Boston took an eight-point lead into the fourth. Pritchard left with a right eye abrasion and did not return."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: BOS 109, MIL 102",
        "text": "The Bucks opened on a 10–4 run, Ryan Rollins's dunks made it 91–89 with 8:17 left, and Nate Ament's layup and free throw gave Milwaukee its first lead, 92–91. White's and-one made it 102–97 with 2:22 left, his five points capped a 7–0 run to 104–97, and George's three restored an eight-point lead. White's free throws sealed it."
      }
    ],
